<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26036" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lā^trōcĭnālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		2. latro, II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to robbers,
				robber-</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				<i>a band of robbers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 125, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">castra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 2</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lă-trōcĭnālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>after the manner of a robber, like a
			robber</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem interimere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6, § 642</span></i>
			.</div>
